            "correct_answer": "The larger angular frequency is $7$, so $e^{j7t}$ rotates faster.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The coefficient of $t$ is the angular rotation rate. Since $7>3$, $e^{j7t}$ turns faster. Both signals are positive-frequency rotations, so both move counterclockwise; the speed comes from the size of $\\omega$.",
